# Unit 06 单词



## controversial
- **音标**: /ˌkɑːntrəˈvɜːrʃl/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 有争议的
- **例句**: The new law is highly controversial.
- **近义词**: debatable, disputed, divisive
- **派生词**: controversy (n.), controversially (adv.)

## conventional
- **音标**: /kənˈvenʃənl/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 传统的；常规的
- **例句**: She has very conventional views on education.
- **近义词**: traditional, standard, orthodox
- **派生词**: convention (n.), unconventional (adj.), conventionally (adv.)

## convert
- **音标**: /kənˈvɜːrt/
- **词性**: v. n.
- **释义**: 转变；转换；改变信仰
- **例句**: They converted the old factory into apartments.
- **近义词**: change, transform, switch
- **派生词**: conversion (n.), convertible (adj. n.)

## convey
- **音标**: /kənˈveɪ/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 传达；运输；表达
- **例句**: Words cannot convey how grateful I am.
- **近义词**: communicate, express, transport
- **派生词**: conveyor (n.)

## convince
- **音标**: /kənˈvɪns/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 使确信；说服
- **例句**: She convinced me to change my mind.
- **近义词**: persuade, assure, satisfy
- **派生词**: conviction (n.), convincing (adj.), convincingly (adv.)

## cooperate
- **音标**: /koʊˈɑːpəreɪt/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 合作；配合
- **例句**: The two companies agreed to cooperate on the project.
- **近义词**: collaborate, work together, team up
- **派生词**: cooperation (n.), cooperative (adj. n.)

## cope
- **音标**: /koʊp/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 应对；处理
- **例句**: She has learned to cope with stress in a healthy way.
- **近义词**: manage, handle, deal with

## core
- **音标**: /kɔːr/
- **词性**: n. adj.
- **释义**: 核心；要点
- **例句**: Trust is the core of any good relationship.
- **近义词**: center, heart, essence

## corporate
- **音标**: /ˈkɔːrpərət/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 公司的；法人的；共同的
- **例句**: The corporate culture emphasizes teamwork.
- **近义词**: business, commercial, organizational
- **派生词**: corporation (n.), corporately (adv.)

## correspond
- **音标**: /ˌkɔːrəˈspɑːnd/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 通信；对应；符合
- **例句**: The two accounts do not correspond with each other.
- **近义词**: match, agree, write to
- **派生词**: correspondence (n.), correspondent (n.), corresponding (adj.)

## corrupt
- **音标**: /kəˈrʌpt/
- **词性**: adj. v.
- **释义**: 腐败的；堕落的；使腐败
- **例句**: The corrupt official was arrested for bribery.
- **近义词**: dishonest, fraudulent, deprave
- **派生词**: corruption (n.), corruptible (adj.)

## counsel
- **音标**: /ˈkaʊnsl/
- **词性**: n. v.
- **释义**: 忠告；律师；建议
- **例句**: The lawyer provided counsel to his client.
- **近义词**: advice, attorney, guidance
- **派生词**: counselor (n.)

## count
- **音标**: /kaʊnt/
- **词性**: v. n.
- **释义**: 计数；重要；指望
- **例句**: Every vote counts in an election.
- **近义词**: calculate, matter, rely on
- **派生词**: countable (adj.), counter (n.), countless (adj.)

## counterpart
- **音标**: /ˈkaʊntərpɑːrt/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 对应的人或物；副本
- **例句**: The CEO met with his Japanese counterpart.
- **近义词**: equivalent, peer, opposite number

## courage
- **音标**: /ˈkɜːrɪdʒ/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 勇气；胆量
- **例句**: It takes courage to stand up for what is right.
- **近义词**: bravery, valor, nerve
- **派生词**: courageous (adj.), encourage (v.), discourage (v.)

## crash
- **音标**: /kræʃ/
- **词性**: v. n.
- **释义**: 碰撞；崩溃；暴跌
- **例句**: The stock market crashed in 2008.
- **近义词**: collide, smash, collapse
- **派生词**: crashing (adj.)

## credit
- **音标**: /ˈkredɪt/
- **词性**: n. v.
- **释义**: 信用；学分；归功于
- **例句**: She deserves credit for her hard work.
- **近义词**: recognition, acknowledgment, trust
- **派生词**: credible (adj.), credential (n.), discredit (v.)

## crisis
- **音标**: /ˈkraɪsɪs/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 危机；关键时刻
- **例句**: The country is facing an economic crisis.
- **近义词**: emergency, disaster, turning point
- **派生词**: critical (adj.)

## critical
- **音标**: /ˈkrɪtɪkl/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 关键的；批评的；危急的
- **例句**: Critical thinking is essential for problem-solving.
- **近义词**: crucial, vital, essential
- **派生词**: critically (adv.), criticism (n.), criticize (v.)

## crucial
- **音标**: /ˈkruːʃl/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 至关重要的；决定性的
- **例句**: This is a crucial moment in the negotiations.
- **近义词**: critical, vital, essential
- **派生词**: crucially (adv.)

## cultivate
- **音标**: /ˈkʌltɪveɪt/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 培养；耕作；栽培
- **例句**: Schools should cultivate students' creativity.
- **近义词**: develop, nurture, foster
- **派生词**: cultivation (n.), cultivated (adj.), cultivator (n.)

## cure
- **音标**: /kjʊr/
- **词性**: n. v.
- **释义**: 治愈；疗法；解决
- **例句**: Scientists are working to find a cure for cancer.
- **近义词**: remedy, heal, treatment
- **派生词**: curable (adj.), incurable (adj.)

## curiosity
- **音标**: /ˌkjʊriˈɑːsəti/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 好奇心；奇物
- **例句**: Children have a natural curiosity about the world.
- **近义词**: inquisitiveness, interest, wonder
- **派生词**: curious (adj.), curiously (adv.)

## current
- **音标**: /ˈkɜːrənt/
- **词性**: adj. n.
- **释义**: 当前的；潮流；电流
- **例句**: The current situation requires immediate action.
- **近义词**: present, contemporary, flow
- **派生词**: currently (adv.), currency (n.)

## curriculum
- **音标**: /kəˈrɪkjələm/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 课程；课程表
- **例句**: The school has revised its curriculum.
- **近义词**: syllabus, program, course of study
- **派生词**: curricula (pl.)

## custom
- **音标**: /ˈkʌstəm/
- **词性**: n. adj.
- **释义**: 习惯；风俗；定制的
- **例句**: It is a custom to eat dumplings during the Spring Festival.
- **近义词**: tradition, habit, practice
- **派生词**: customary (adj.), customer (n.), customize (v.)

## cycle
- **音标**: /ˈsaɪkl/
- **词性**: n. v.
- **释义**: 循环；周期；骑自行车
- **例句**: The business cycle affects the economy significantly.
- **近义词**: rotation, round, bicycle
- **派生词**: cyclic (adj.), cyclical (adj.), recycle (v.)

## damage
- **音标**: /ˈdæmɪdʒ/
- **词性**: n. v.
- **释义**: 损害；损坏
- **例句**: The storm caused severe damage to the buildings.
- **近义词**: harm, destruction, injury
- **派生词**: damaging (adj.)

## data
- **音标**: /ˈdeɪtə/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 数据；资料
- **例句**: The data shows a significant increase in sales.
- **近义词**: information, statistics, facts
- **派生词**: database (n.)

## deadline
- **音标**: /ˈdedlaɪn/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 截止日期；最后期限
- **例句**: The deadline for the project is next Friday.
- **近义词**: due date, time limit, cutoff

## debate
- **音标**: /dɪˈbeɪt/
- **词性**: n. v.
- **释义**: 辩论；讨论
- **例句**: The candidates engaged in a heated debate.
- **近义词**: discussion, argument, dispute
- **派生词**: debatable (adj.), debater (n.)
